  "query_preview": "(This evening through Friday)...\nIssued at 206 PM EST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nRest of This Afternoon through Saturday...\n\nSome patchy light rain continues across portions of the eastern \nforecast area early this afternoon. Some additional lake enhanced \nshowers were across northern Indiana, moving southeast. Will keep \nsome low PoPs going this afternoon, mainly northeast. By evening, \nflow will have changed enough that odds of lake enhanced showers \nentering the forecast area will be too low to mention.\n\nDrier air continues to erode the clouds across the western and far \nnorthern forecast area. This trend will continue through the \nafternoon. Additional clouds were drifting south from Lake Michigan. \nThe end result by late afternoon will mostly clear to partly cloudy \nacross the southwest half of the area with partly to mostly cloudy \nnortheast half.\n\nTonight into Saturday morning, additional forcing and moisture \nwrapping around an upper low will keep a cloud deck across the \nnortheast half or so of the forecast area, making skies partly to \nmostly cloudy. To the southwest, skies will be mostly clear to \npartly cloudy. These conditions will allow the southwest half to end \nup a little cooler than the northeast half tonight. Lows southwest \nwill be around 30 with lower 30s northeast.\n\nSaturday afternoon, the upper low will move east, taking the lower \nclouds with it. However, some high clouds will move in from the \nwest. Highs will be in the lower 50s. If lower clouds take longer to \nexit or higher clouds are thicker than expected, readings could be a \nfew degrees cooler.\n\nSunday through Wednesday...\n\nCentral Indiana will remain in northwest flow aloft through \nWednesday, between upper systems moving to the north and south of \nthe area. Any forcing that does sneak into the area won't have any \nmoisture to work with, so will go dry through Wednesday. \nTemperatures will moderate into the lower and middle 60s by Tuesday, \nbut some slightly cooler air will move in for Wednesday, but highs \nwill still be around 60 to the lower 60s.\n\nThursday and Friday...\n\nAn upper trough will bring in cooler air to the end of next week. It \nmay squeeze out some light rain on Thursday. Highs will be in the \n50s, with lows returning to near freezing.",
